{"name":"Codium Fragile","hex":"#524b2a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily broken, not sturdy; of delicate material.","Readily disrupted or destroyed."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that is fragile."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Codium fragile","blocks":[{"text":"Codium fragile, known commonly as green sea fingers, dead man's fingers, felty fingers, forked felt-alga, stag seaweed, sponge seaweed, green sponge, green fleece, sea staghorn, and oyster thief, is a species of seaweed in the family Codiaceae. It originates in the Pacific Ocean near Japan and has become an invasive species on the coasts of the Northern Atlantic Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Dead_Man%27s_Fingers_%28Codium_fragile%29_-_Tor_Bay_Provincial_Park%2C_Nova_Scotia_2022-07-27_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Dead_Man%27s_Fingers_%28Codium_fragile%29_-_Tor_Bay_Provincial_Park%2C_Nova_Scotia_2022-07-27_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codium_fragile","wikidata":"Q2712208"},{"title":"Codium","blocks":[{"text":"Codium is a genus of edible green macroalgae under the order Bryopsidales. The genus name is derived from a Greek word that pertains to the soft texture of its thallus. One of the foremost experts on Codium taxonomy was Paul Claude Silva at the University of California, Berkeley. Silva was able to describe 36 species for the genus, and in honor of his work on Codium, the species C. silvae was named after him."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Codium_sp..jpg/330px-Codium_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codium","wikidata":"Q1143304"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Dea